# The halium initramfs starts recovery's init at its second stage, which reads
# neither prop.halium nor init.recovery.${ro.hardware}.rc (ro.hardware is not
# set yet), so the settings for the system-image upgrader are set here.
#
# Ubuntu Touch is installed into system_b, grown to 4500 MB first. super
# (8.7 GB) only has room for that without the stock Android system partitions,
# which Ubuntu Touch does not use; vendor_a (the drivers) is kept. They are
# removed from the partition tables of both slots, so a slot a boot cannot
# reuse their space.
on init
    setprop ro.systemimage.system_partition_size 4500
    setprop ro.systemimage.remove_dynparts_slot_a system_a,system_ext_a
    setprop ro.systemimage.remove_dynparts_slot_b system_a,system_ext_a
